---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '2026-10-21';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Content Update Log"
  description="Dated record of VisaLang editorial deepenings, source rechecks, and isolation changes—without inventing personal credentials."
  canonicalURL="https://visalang.org/content-update-log/"
  noindex={false}
  enableAds={false}
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <article class="guide-article narrow-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Trust</p>
      <h1>Content Update Log</h1>
      <p class="guide-summary">This log lists substantive editorial work and source-review hygiene. It is not a promise that every time-sensitive fee, seat, or acceptance fact remains current. Always re-check the responsible authority, exam owner, and authorised centre before you pay or file.</p>

      <h2>How to read this log</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Deepening</strong> means unique decision help was added or rewritten (decision trees, responsibility splits, checklists, comparison tables, scenario pitfalls, or record templates).</li>
        <li><strong>Source recheck</strong> means official URLs were opened again and claims were kept or adjusted; a date-only recheck is labelled as such.</li>
        <li><strong>Isolation</strong> means a page stays reachable by URL but remains outside primary discovery, sitemap advertising eligibility, or both until it meets maturity standards.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2026-10-21 — AdSense P0 depth remediation (Germany A1/B1)</h2>
      <p>Editorial deepening for the auditable Germany double-route sample. Authority-First boundaries unchanged; no fabricated fees, seats, acceptance outcomes, or personal professional credentials.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A1 Route Hub</strong> (<a href="/germany-family-reunion-a1/">/germany-family-reunion-a1/</a>): decision order, responsibility split, route pitfalls, minimum record template.</li>
        <li><strong>A1 core supports deepened:</strong> <a href="/guides/german-family-reunion-language-requirement/">language requirement</a>, <a href="/guides/goethe-a1-germany-family-reunion/">Goethe A1 proof fit</a>, <a href="/guides/goethe-a1-vs-telc-a1/">Goethe vs telc</a>, <a href="/guides/german-a1-documents-checklist/">documents checklist</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>B1 Route Hub</strong> (<a href="/germany-b1-settlement-citizenship/">/germany-b1-settlement-citizenship/</a>): settlement vs citizenship decision order, responsibility split, pitfalls, record template.</li>
        <li><strong>B1 hardcore supports deepened:</strong> <a href="/guides/goethe-b1-germany-settlement-work/">settlement procedure</a>, <a href="/guides/germany-b1-citizenship-language-proof/">citizenship language proof / acceptance framing</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Trust pages:</strong> Editorial Method strengthened on About / Editorial Policy; this Update Log published; footer link added.</li>
        <li><strong>Isolation / ads:</strong> pending and starter pages remain fail-closed (noindex + no AdSense loader in primary discovery); commercial coming-soon shells stay noindex and out of sitemap.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Earlier windows (summary)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>2026-07 to 2026-08:</strong> Window A/B advertising inventory closure; international thin clusters held as Official Verification Navigator pages (noindex, no ads).</li>
        <li><strong>2026-07-19 / 2026-07-22 / 2026-08-15:</strong> Germany A1/B1 source-review batches and FAN-42 requirement recheck (see individual guide <code>sourceReviewedAt</code> fields).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>If you find an outdated official link or a wording conflict, use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with the page URL and the official source. We log corrections after checking the source hierarchy in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.</p>

      <p class="compliance-line">VisaLang is independent and informational. Bylines such as “Editorial team” describe work roles, not lawyer, immigration-adviser, or exam-board credentials.</p>
      <p class="last-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
